{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban unattended parcel deliveries without consent & make courier liable for loss",
        "additional_details": "UK businesses pay couriers to deliver goods safely, yet when parcels are abandoned and stolen, retailers usually bear the cost of refunds, replacements and redelivery. In our view, a doorstep photo is not proof of delivery. We fail to understand why businesses should so often pay for courier failures. We demand a law holding courier companies financially liable for unauthorised deliveries. It's time to end this unfair practice - protect small businesses, hold couriers accountable and stop making retailers pay for their mistakes!",
        "background": "Introduce legislation making it illegal for couriers to leave parcels unattended without the recipient\u2019s explicit consent. Hold courier companies legally liable for parcels stolen, lost or damaged as a result of unauthorised deliveries, with mandatory compensation and penalties for breaches.",
